  "details": "Using \"VRCStation set PlayerMobility\" node cause assembly error:\n    Type referenced by 'VRCSDKBaseVRCStationMobility' could not be resolved.\n\nIt also floods error spams on the Console while the Inspector shows Udon graph asset.\n\nTested with: VRCSDK3-UDON-2020.04.09.16.59_Public\n\n----\nDetails:\nGenerated assembly contains:\n>    Mobility_0: %VRCSDKBaseVRCStationMobility, null\nThis line cause the error.\n\nSame issue occurs for \"VRCPickup set AutoHold\" node. It generates\n>    AutoHoldMode_0: %VRCSDKBaseVRC_PickupAutoHoldMode, null\nAnd it cause:\n>    Type referenced by 'VRCSDKBaseVRC_PickupAutoHoldMode' could not be resolved.\n\nBoth are nested types in C#. Inspector shows their types in DataTypeString as\n>    VRC.SDKBase.VRCStation+Mobility, VRCSDKBase##0\n>    VRC.SDKBase.VRC_Pickup+AutoHoldMode, VRCSDKBase##0\n\nSo I guess actual issue is \"nested types could not be resolved\".",
